  "2026-07-10T10:47:37.642Z",maintainer-agent,"Evidence 2026-07-10: validate_resolution_missing_fields drifted 269 -> 272 (+3) in one day — the 2026-07-09 closes of pm-2ldo, pm-q6gx, pm-cu1i (all closed via close -m with strong prose close_reason but no structured resolution/expected/actual). Confirms the faucet is every routine agent close, not a legacy backlog: without a close-time signal the structured fields will keep losing to close_reason. Rate data point for prioritization: ~3/day at current agent throughput."
  "2026-07-10T16:20:54.345Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet evidence 2026-07-10 (post PR #499): validate_resolution_missing_fields 272 -> 277. The +5 are the schema-fidelity bundle closures (pm-kfq5, pm-l6rz, pm-zazb, pm-b84u, pm-ghf1) — all closed with a substantive close_reason but no structured resolution/expected/actual triple, exactly the leak this item gates. Third consecutive pass with growth (269 -> 272 -> 277); each shipped lane adds ~5. Other buckets steady: missing_linked_paths 154, orphaned_paths 124, missing_close_reason 18 (pm-e9zh), duplicate_issue_codes 1 (pm-pivf)."
  "2026-07-10T21:27:42.513Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet evidence 2026-07-10 (post-PR#502): resolution_missing_fields 277 -> 278 (+1). The lane closed 8 items (pm-114v/l0bu/yl6c/hfg5/ol5v/6y58/z32q/w7jq) but only +1 leaked — close reasons were set on all 8; the +1 is a partial-fields close. Rate is falling versus the ~+5/lane baseline, but the faucet is still open until the close-time completeness gate ships."
  "2026-07-11T02:51:16.306Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet evidence 2026-07-11: resolution_missing_fields HELD at 278 across PR#506's nine closes (pm-4ak1/5566/2vb2/768v/m0uc/mswi/qely/uwu0/uxmf) — first fully zero-leak lane observed (trend: +5/lane pre-#47, +1/8 on PR#502, 0/9 now). Close-time completeness discipline is landing without the gate; remaining 278 is legacy stock, so this item's value is now mostly ratchet-protection (prevent regression) + backfill, not stemming an active faucet."
  "2026-07-11T09:56:18.352Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet trend update 2026-07-11 (post-PR#511): resolution_missing_fields HELD at 278 across 4 more lane closes (pm-s9iu/pm-0mjz/pm-o71e/pm-9qcr, all with structured resolutions) — SECOND consecutive zero-leak lane after PR#506's 9 closes. Two independent lanes now demonstrate close-time completeness is achievable by default; ratchet gate (fail on any increase above 278) is de-risked, remaining value is the legacy backfill half."
  "2026-07-11T16:06:23.750Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet evidence 2026-07-11 (PR#512 lane): 7/7 closes leaked structured resolution fields (je50/d30l/zuw8/9ugc/qd2h/ypha/pmmv had close_reason only; resolution/expected/actual absent) — first leak after two consecutive zero-leak lanes (PR#506 0/9, PR#511 0/4). Trend 278->285, backfilled same day by maintainer-agent -> back to 278. Lane authors codex-root + maintainer-agent used pm close -m without pm update structured fields. Confirms close-time completeness gate (this item) is still the missing control: zero-leak lanes were author discipline, not tooling."
  "2026-07-11T22:53:19.500Z",maintainer-agent,"PR#517 lane (2026-07-11, 5 closes): 3/5 complete at close (pm-fjxm/pm-1mwk/pm-eqk0), 2/5 leaked resolution fields (pm-7rlp, pm-krwu — both chores) — backfilled same-day by maintainer-agent. Running pattern holds: feature/issue closes carry the triple, chore closes leak it; the close-time completeness gate this item owns remains the missing control. Trend count stays 278 (chore leak apparently outside validate's resolution check scope — worth covering in the gate)."
  "2026-07-12T06:11:45.055Z",maintainer-agent,"PR#520 lane (merged 2026-07-12): 5/5 closes leaked the resolution triple (pm-b9ov, pm-dprb, pm-b0se, pm-jw2a, pm-sjfs — all Issue-type) — backfilled same-day by maintainer-agent. This refutes the pass-#68 pattern that only CHORE closes leak: issue closes leak too when the closing agent skips the fields. Close-time completeness gate remains the missing control; author discipline does not scale across lanes."
  "2026-07-12T08:26:40.933Z",maintainer-agent,"Trend point 2026-07-12 (post-PR#523): missing_resolution_fields 278 -> 276. Delta = legacy set shrinking via the same-day PR#517-lane backfills (pm-7rlp, pm-krwu) which landed after the last 278 measurement; verified none of the recent lane ids (PR#517/#520/#523 closes) appear in the 276 rows — close-time discipline holding, count now moving for the first time since #57. Gate remains the missing control."
  "2026-07-12T11:57:12.089Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet evidence 2026-07-12 (post-#72 pass): PR#524 lane closed pm-a2h3 WITHOUT the resolution triple -> trend 276->277; backfilled same day by maintainer-agent (fixed / parity-expected / PR#524-shipped), trend back to 276. Running leak record: PR#506 0/9, PR#511 0/4, PR#512 7/7 (backfilled), PR#517-lane legacy backfills -2, PR#524 1/1 (backfilled). Close-time completeness gate remains the missing control."
  "2026-07-12T18:53:41.662Z",maintainer-agent,"Faucet evidence 2026-07-12 (pass #74): PR#525 lane closed 4 items (pm-mi2x, pm-dfg0, pm-1ybs, pm-bl8x) with FULL resolution triples — zero-leak lane, author discipline again (gate still the missing control). validate resolution_missing_fields steady at 276."
  "2026-07-13T08:59:02.892Z",maintainer-agent,"Trend (pass #76, 2026-07-13): 276 → 279 → 276. PR#536 self-closed 9 lane items and leaked the resolution triple on 3/9 (pm-vjk3, pm-rxp1, pm-w1c0 — Feature/Task/Plan; the 6 Tasks with resolution were fine); backfilled same-day by maintainer-agent. Author discipline again, not tooling — the close-time completeness gate this item owns remains the missing control."
  "2026-07-28T10:37:06.472Z","harness:claude-code","Faucet reading 2026-07-28: `validate_resolution_missing_fields` = **291**.\n\nTrend across recorded measurements: 269 → 272 → 277 → 278 → 278 → 278 → 278 → 276 → **291**. The 276 reading was the first downward movement and was attributed to legacy-set shrinkage via post-measurement backfills; this is a +15 reversal, the largest single jump in the series.\n\nThat direction matters more than the magnitude. Every prior increase was traced to a specific PR-lane leak and backfilled the same day by author discipline, which is exactly the argument this item makes — the gate is still the missing control, and the one time discipline lapses the number moves 15 at once. A +15 excursion is not consistent with the legacy set, which only shrinks; it is new closures landing without the resolution triple.\n\nNext step before any backfill: attribute the delta to closures rather than assuming legacy, so the backfill does not paper over a lane that is still leaking.\n"
  "2026-07-28T15:05:23.511Z","harness:claude-code","Faucet re-measured 2026-07-28: validate_resolution_missing_fields is 291, continuing the trend 269, 272, 277, 278 held for five passes, 276, 279, 276, and now 291. The step of roughly fifteen since 2026-07-13 tracks the lane volume of the last two weeks rather than a change in discipline, and the close-time completeness gate this item owns remains the missing control. Also re-confirmed this pass: Chore closes missing the triple still do not move the count, so the check's scope exclusion noted earlier is unchanged."
  "2026-08-31T22:36:36.702Z","harness:codex","Implementation start from CodeRabbit comment 3899001134: existing pm close already accepts resolution, expected, and actual in one atomic close mutation and the default governance preset warns when they are missing. Add an explicit immutable-history regression proving those fields are present on the close event itself, strengthen agent workflow guidance to record structured fields before close, and preserve the historical pm-ka6d stream append-only."
  "2026-08-31T22:41:04.651Z","harness:codex","Implementation progress: generated and repository guidance now place resolution, expected, and actual on the pm close invocation itself. A new sandboxed integration test reads the raw append-only history stream and proves the one close event contains all three structured values plus the terminal status, with no later backfill event. Existing warn/strict/default governance behavior remains unchanged."
  "2026-08-31T23:05:42.744Z","harness:codex","Terminal evidence: the linked close-history and generated-guidance suite passed 43 tests. A manual isolated-workspace acceptance created and strictly closed pm-8my1, then verified the single final close event contains resolution, expected_result, actual_result, and status. Repository-wide 8,204-test exact coverage, static quality, secret scan, and dependency audit passed."
  "2026-09-01T02:55:14.232Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence: CodeRabbit comment 3900091404 correctly observes that the existing implementation tests cover warn, require, and complete-field silence but the PM item links only the immutable close-event cohort. Link and run the focused close command and CLI integration evidence before re-closing."
  "2026-09-01T03:17:05.866Z","harness:codex","Terminal acceptance evidence: both linked cohorts passed. The immutable close-event and generated guidance cohort passed 43 tests; the focused close-command and CLI cohort passed 152 tests covering warn output, strict refusal with recovery, and zero warnings when all structured fields are supplied."
