  "2026-07-17T04:44:37.677Z",maintainer-agent,"Leak evidence pass #94 (2026-07-17): PR#575 lane (codex-wide-sdk-20260716) self-closed pm-qfdd/pm-cbwg/pm-w89s ALL without the resolution triple — third lane occurrence (PR#512, PR#536, PR#573/oslr precedents); backfilled same-day by maintainer-agent. Close-time completeness gate remains the missing control. SCOPE ANOMALY (second observation): these three leaked closes did NOT bump validate's missing_resolution_items (stayed 276), while pm-oslr's identical leak in pass #93 DID bump it to 277 — the counting scope is inconsistent across closes (first observation was Chore closes not bumping the then-278). Gate design should count from close-op field presence, not whatever the current scope filter is."
  "2026-07-25T07:17:26.333Z","harness:claude-code","Faucet trend update (ecosystem review 2026-07-25): validate_resolution_missing_fields moved 278 -> 287 since the last recorded reading. The nine-row increase accumulated across the 2026-07-22 to 2026-07-25 lanes rather than in a single close, so it is ordinary faucet drift rather than one leaky PR; the close-time completeness gate this item owns remains the missing control. Recorded as a change datapoint per the drift convention — no repair performed on closed holders (changelog drag), and no new item filed."
  "2026-07-25T20:42:24.563Z","harness:claude-code","Faucet reading 2026-07-25: validate_resolution_missing_fields is 287, up from the 278 that held from pass-era measurements through 2026-07-15, with the rows array no longer truncated so the whole set is enumerable.\n\nEleven of the 287 are recent closes rather than the legacy set, all from the 2026-07-21 to 2026-07-23 window, listed newest first with their closed_at: pm-llrp 07-23T16:00:02, pm-g072 07-23T16:00:01, pm-nf7q 07-23T15:50:18, pm-853a 07-23T15:37:28, pm-4v4c 07-23T15:37:27, pm-l98s 07-23T14:39:27, pm-v3zd3o 07-23T07:56:34, pm-fgih 07-23T07:56:33, pm-5qmm 07-23T07:56:31, pm-ju83 07-22T21:36:22, pm-bnmlsc 07-21T22:11:15. Every one is missing the full triple (resolution, expected_result, actual_result) except pm-0pnz and pm-13nx in the legacy set, which are missing only the two result fields.\n\nDeliberately not backfilled here. These closed two to four days ago and were bucketed into their release sections by updated_at; touching them now would move them into the current unreleased bucket and produce changelog drift for work that already shipped. That is exactly the reason a close-time gate rather than periodic backfill is the fix this item owns — the same eleven items would have cost nothing to complete at close time.\n\nContrast with the 2026-07-25 lane closed by PR#713: pm-qwuber, pm-03pq3o, pm-6uxhe0, pm-zqsrt5, pm-sx52hr, and pm-brxdct all carry resolution and close_reason, so the leak is not uniform across authors or lanes — which is the pattern the gate has to make irrelevant."
  "2026-07-25T21:42:44.253Z","harness:claude-code","Faucet reading 2026-07-25 (evening, post-2026.7.25 build review): validate_resolution_missing_fields is 287, against the 276-278 band this item has tracked since 2026-07-12. The trend is upward again, consistent with the closing activity in the 07-21..25 window rather than with any new leak class. Recording the number only; the count-side gate this item owns is unchanged and no closed items were touched to produce it."
